Z||000006||rockcrawl||05-21-2001||06:25 PM||||I'll probably attempt to make my own, I was just wondering if they were home made or if someone is manufacturing them. They were very high quality. The lettering and arrowhead appeared to be "molded in" although it must have been silkscreened on the back. They did not appear to be attached over the original frame, but rather a complete replacement. The edges had a rolled look just like fastback windows. It gives the car a much cleaner look. <P>Every time I was near that car, the owner wasn't around, and before I knew it the day was over.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Only thing it covers is the vent for the interior.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>I thought of that but I don't think it's a problem. The fastback windows don't have vents.||||reg||1
